# Own domains (item 21c, D153). Imported by the server's main Caddyfile with
# `import /etc/caddy/sites/habre-cms-own-domains.caddy`, and only once that
# Caddyfile's global options hold the ask endpoint:
#
#   {
#   	on_demand_tls {
#   		ask http://127.0.0.1:3000/_caddy/ask
#   	}
#   }
#
# deploy/setup-server.sh installs this file always, but adds the import line
# only when the main Caddyfile already names /_caddy/ask - so it can never
# switch on-demand certificates on without the check in front of them. The
# global option is the server owner's change (needs-you.md), because the
# repository does not own the main Caddyfile.
#
# What it does: a customer's own domain is any name not matched by the
# explicit blocks in habre-cms.caddy. Caddy asks the app before it gets a
# certificate for a new name; the app answers 200 only for a verified domain
# of a site that is not suspended (app/features/own-domain/caddy-ask.ts), so
# a stranger pointing a name at this server cannot make it request one.
#
# (habre_cms_proxy) is the snippet defined in habre-cms.caddy.

https:// {
	tls {
		on_demand
	}
	import habre_cms_proxy habre-cms-public-access
}

# A visitor typing the plain http address of an own domain reaches https. Named
# hosts elsewhere in the Caddyfile keep their own automatic redirect; this
# block only answers names nothing else matched.
http:// {
	redir https://{host}{uri} permanent
}
